  "title": "Battle of Bannockburn",
  "summary": "Over two days in June 1314, near Stirling, Robert the Bruce's Scottish army defeated a larger English army led by Edward II, which had come to relieve the besieged Stirling Castle. Edward fled by boat, and the victory gave Bruce effective control of Scotland, though the war lasted another fourteen years.",
